      "name": "What is paper honeycomb board?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Paper honeycomb board is a sandwich material made of a hexagonal kraft-paper core glued between two flat paper liners. The hexagonal geometry — the same structure bees use — gives it an exceptional strength-to-weight ratio: rigid enough to replace plywood in pallets, crates, and panels while weighing up to 80% less." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is honeycomb board made?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Kraft paper sheets are glued in offset lines, stacked, pressed, and cut into slices. Each slice is then expanded like an accordion into a hexagonal-cell core, dried for stability, and laminated between top and bottom liner sheets to form a rigid sandwich board." }
